{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 4, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "i recently watched \"the social network\" and was thoroughly impressed by the film's intricate storytelling, complex characters, and outstanding performances. directed by david fincher, the movie tells the story of facebook's founding and the subsequent legal battles that ensued.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard, creating a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. after the site becomes a huge hit, mark is accused of violating students' privacy and is brought before the harvard administrative board.\n\nsoon after, mark is approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who claim that mark had agreed to help them create a social networking site called \"harvard connect.\" mark allegedly steals their idea and creates his own site, \"thefacebook,\" with the help of his friend eduardo savernin (played by andrew garfield).\n\nas the site gains popularity, mark and eduardo's friendship begins to fray, and they find themselves at odds over the direction of the company. meanwhile, the winklevoss twins become increasingly determined to sue mark for allegedly stealing their idea.\n\none of the standout aspects of \"the social network\" is its nuanced portrayal of mark zuckerberg. eisenberg's performance is remarkable, capturing the complexities and contradictions of mark's character. he is depicted as a brilliant programmer, but also as a socially awkward and vindictive individual who is driven by a desire for success and recognition.\n\nthe supporting cast is equally impressive, with garfield delivering a standout performance as eduardo savernin. the chemistry between eisenberg and garfield is palpable, and their portrayal of the complicated friendship between mark and eduardo is both convincing and heartbreaking.\n\nthe film's cinematography is also noteworthy, with fincher's signature dark and moody aesthetic perfectly capturing the atmosphere of harvard's elite social scene. the score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is equally effective, adding to the film's tense and unsettling atmosphere.\n\none of the most striking aspects of \"the social network\" is its exploration of the themes of ambition, friendship, and the consequences of success. the film raises important questions about the ethics of entrepreneurship and the costs of achieving greatness.\n\noverall, \"the social network\" is a thought-provoking and engaging film that is both a fascinating character study and a compelling drama. with its intricate storytelling, complex characters, and outstanding performances, it is a must-see for anyone interested in the story behind one of the world's most influential companies.", "logprobs": [{"token": "i", "logprob": -1.883251667022705}, {"token": " recently", "logprob": -0.011960811913013458}, {"token": " watched", "logprob": -0.07889106869697571}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.001604580320417881}, {"token": "the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " social", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.018149960786104202}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.011054699309170246}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.22115755081176758}, {"token": " thoroughly", "logprob": -0.0015236446633934975}, {"token": " impressed", "logprob": -2.1219027985353023e-05}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.0015028145862743258}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0067427014000713825}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.000979539705440402}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -2.753696753643453e-05}, {"token": " intricate", "logprob": -1.169087290763855}, {"token": " storytelling", "logprob": -0.030332988128066063}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.07888974994421005}, {"token": " complex", "logprob": -0.12244663387537003}, {"token": "